.policy "ruff-g004-logging-f-string" revision 2
.description "Pass values to a logging call as arguments instead of interpolating them into an f-string message; the logger then formats only records it emits."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff G004 (flake8-logging-format): a logging call whose message is an f-string, or adjacent literals one of
// which is. Pass the values as the call's arguments instead; the logger formats them only for records it emits.
// A t-string is not an f-string. The message is the first argument (the second for `log`) or `msg=`. Reported at
// the message. (Ruff's fix is preview-only, so none here.)
//   logging.info(f"Hello {name}")                    ← G004
//   logging.info(f"no placeholders")                 ← G004
//   info(t"{name}")                                  not reported: a template string
#include "python/logging.rr"

.violation G004(at: node) code "G004"
    "Replace the f-string with a `%s` format string and pass its values as logger arguments, e.g. `logger.info(\"x=%s\", x)`, doubling any literal `%`; leave it if the logger is not from `logging`."
    suppress ruff "G004"
G004(e) :- log_msg(_, e), fstring(e).
